{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>An abode, the God of old.</b> The heavens are the abode of the Holy One, blessed be He, who precedes all things." "<b>And beneath, arms of eternity etc.</b> And beneath the heavens He rules, as over the supernal beings, and He is the strength and might of the world, for He rules the world below and above." "<b>And He shall drive the enemy from before you.</b> All your enemies from before Him." "<b>And He said: Destroy.</b> And He said to me: Destroy your enemy, as we find regarding Amalek, that He commanded ״תמחה את זכר עמלק״, and likewise regarding the Canaanite: ״לא תחיה כל נשמה״. ״וישכן ישראל בטח בדד״ — all those who are of the עין of Jacob are His, that is, his own עין, such as righteous converts — they shall dwell safely and apart; in their joy no stranger shall intermingle. And so Balaam said: ״הן עם לבדד ישכון ובגוים לא יתחשב״. But the heretics and the informers and those who deliver Jews over to the authorities and those who secede from the ways of the community shall not dwell with them, for it was not said זרע יעקב but rather עין יעקב."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:10.565048428Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}